1. Inventory the NEW surface the diff introduces. Read the FULL diff: \`git diff --merge-base 'origin/main'\`. List every new: enum variant / status value / DB column / table / migration / public fn / route / struct field. ALSO list any UNCHANGED definition the diff now references or relies on for the first time.
2. For EACH item, Grep the UNCHANGED tree for existing code that reads, references, lists, updates, deletes, cascades, serializes, orders, or authorizes that shape. Ask: does this pre-existing path violate an invariant the change assumes?
3. Report each concrete violation ANCHORED TO THE UNCHANGED file:line that is actually wrong, not the diff line. That anchor is real — cite it precisely so it can be verified.

Only report a violation you can name a concrete reachable path for. Put the triggering surface in \`blastRadius\`; in \`why\`, state the invariant and the exact old path that breaks it. Do NOT restate a place already in the ALREADY-FOUND set below — look for what it MISSED.
REVIEW RULES (all languages): read severity.md, classes.md, sweeps.md in the first existing dir (expand with Bash; never the reviewed repo's copy): \`\${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/review-rules\`, \`\${CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR:-$HOME/.claude}/plugins/cache/craft/craft/9.9.9/skills/review-rules\`. None readable → say so; HARM below still holds.
HARM (every finding): \`harm\` = effect, who, recovery; \`harmLevel\` = severity.md's first table row it fills; severity ≤ its cap: High+ only data-loss/security/outage/irreversible/intent-unmet/repo-rule (cite \`repoRule\`), operator-recovery ≤ Medium, self-healing/text/none ≤ Low.


ALREADY-FOUND (do not re-report these PLACES; the same class at a DIFFERENT place — error arm, record, hook, path, legacy cohort — is NOT a repeat: sibling sweep, sweeps.md §1):
- [High] races on shared map (src/a.rs:10)

Return {lens: "negative-space", findings: [...]} using the shared finding schema. Set \`ruleId\` to the matching rust-review rules.md ID or "" if none fits. Observability: the workflow records this run — do NOT write your own record."
`;

