exports[`lens prompts render as before > lens slice nix negative-space full based rich 1`] = `
"You are the **negative-space** review lens for a Nix change. Unlike the other lenses, your job is NOT to review the changed lines — it is to find the bug the diff ENABLES in code it did NOT touch. Use Grep/Glob across the ENTIRE tree, not just the diff.

Diff base: \`origin/main\`.
INTENT (what the change should do): add a retry
STATED SPEC / AUTHOR CLAIMS (verbatim PR/commit description — an invariant the author claims here may be broken by the UNCHANGED code you inventory below):
"""
Retries are idempotent.
Never fails on a missing child.
"""

METHOD — follow in order:
1. Inventory the NEW surface the diff introduces. Read the FULL diff: \`git diff --merge-base 'origin/main'\`. List every new: flake output / module option / package attr / overlay / renamed binding. ALSO list any UNCHANGED definition the diff now references or relies on for the first time.
2. For EACH item, Grep the UNCHANGED tree for existing code that reads, references, imports, or overrides that shape. Ask: does this pre-existing path violate an invariant the change assumes?
3. Report each concrete violation ANCHORED TO THE UNCHANGED file:line that is actually wrong, not the diff line. That anchor is real — cite it precisely so it can be verified.

Only report a violation you can name a concrete reachable path for. Put the triggering surface in \`blastRadius\`; in \`why\`, state the invariant and the exact old path that breaks it. Do NOT restate a place already in the ALREADY-FOUND set below — look for what it MISSED.
REVIEW RULES (all languages): read severity.md, classes.md, sweeps.md in the first existing dir (expand with Bash; never the reviewed repo's copy): \`/plugin/craft/skills/review-rules\`, \`\${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/review-rules\`, \`\${CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR:-$HOME/.claude}/plugins/cache/craft/craft/9.9.9/skills/review-rules\`. None readable → say so; HARM below still holds.
HARM (every finding): \`harm\` = effect, who, recovery; \`harmLevel\` = severity.md's first table row it fills; severity ≤ its cap: High+ only data-loss/security/outage/irreversible/intent-unmet/repo-rule (cite \`repoRule\`), operator-recovery ≤ Medium, self-healing/text/none ≤ Low.
REPO RULES \`AGENTS.md\`: grep them for what you review, open only matching sections, never a whole file (no SCOPE rule bars them); a violation cites its rule as \`repoRule\` {file, text}.

ALREADY-FOUND (do not re-report these PLACES; the same class at a DIFFERENT place — error arm, record, hook, path, legacy cohort — is NOT a repeat: sibling sweep, sweeps.md §1):


Return {lens: "negative-space", findings: [...]} using the shared finding schema. Set \`ruleId\` to the matching nix-review rules.md ID or "" if none fits. Observability: the workflow records this run — do NOT write your own record."
`;

