  at src/a.rs:12
  why: deadlock under load
  source: concurrency · rule CON-002
  off-site evidence claimed: src/b.rs:40 the caller
  harm claimed (worst first; effect, who, recovery): outage: the service hangs; every client; operator restart

MECHANICAL CHECK FIRST: if a tool can decide this finding (a clippy lint, statix/deadnix rule, semgrep rule, cargo-audit advisory — infer from source/ruleId/title), RUN it scoped to the cited file; its output overrides your judgement in BOTH directions: tool still reports it → refuted=false; tool demonstrably no longer reports it → refuted=true (quote the output in reason). The gate invoked the tools as: "clippy via CI #12 local" — if a tool is not on PATH, reproduce the gate's invocation (e.g. \`nix run nixpkgs#<tool> --\`) before declaring it unrunnable. If you STILL cannot run the tool, set refuted=false — an unverifiable tool finding stays alive.

